New Game:     Relly Clever Solutions -- Breaking butterflies 
              on the wheel in nethack  


Idea:  Choose a simple problem with well--known solutions, and 
provide an alternate solution with an absurd amount of effort 
and some obviously braindead tactics involved.  



Example:  


Problem:  Get a BoH uncursed when it's too heavy to dip 
into holy water, but still liftable for you ('overtaxed'), 
and there's an altar on the same level.  

Boring Standard Solution:  /oCancellation.  

Assumption:  Nymphs can steal such a heavy BoH. (I don't 
have wizmode at hand to check, sorry, but glancing quickly 
at the source comments of steal.c I didn't find a reason 
why not.  But CMIIW.)  

Solution:  

- Step 1:  Genocide all dwarves and Umber hulks, then 
           magic-map the level.  

- Step 2:  Fill the level with boulders, except for four 
           squares (bag square, one adjacent, altar, one 
           adjacent).  
 
- Step 3:  Wish for a cursed figurine of a nymph.  

- Step 4:  Stand on the square with the bag, drop all 
           possesions, pick up figurine, apply figurine 
           to the square next to you, pick up bag.  Now 
           the nymph should steal the bag and teleport 
           away.  

- Step 5:  Use controlled teleport and try to port on the 
           square adjacent to the altar, until it succeeds.  
           (You can also check with telepathy where the 
           nymph is.)  The nymph should stand on the altar 
           by now.  

- Step 6:  Kill the nymph, and start a sacc-praying combo 
           (picking the BoH up before each prayer) until 
           you get your possesions uncursed.  

Come to think of it, one can extend this solution to a 
possibly-working one if there's no altar on the level:  
First, explore the dungeon below until you find some altar 
reachable by stairs or portals (that's the possibly-working 
part of it).  Then fill all intermediate levels with boulders, 
leaving only up/downstairs and one adjacent square free (nymphs 
do flee downstairs, don't they?).  Chase the nymph downstairs 
similarly to the above chase-to-altar method.  


